# Step over through the loop of accumulate() (demo.c:31-32) on the flash demo (start it first
# with start_in_flash): `for (i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += scale(i, 3);` with n = 4.
#
# The condition i < n sits after the body, so from it the loop branches back. Step over has to
# stop in the body again with i = 1; it used to run on to the end of the loop (i = 4) because it
# only stopped at the next statement by address (fixed in the probe-rs fork).

attach ${ATTACH:-../../dap-client/examples/tc275_demo_3cores.json}
pause all
break ${AURIX_DEMO:-C:/work/aurix_tcf_demo}/src/demo.c:32 if i == 0
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason breakpoint
expect i == 0
unbreak ${AURIX_DEMO:-C:/work/aurix_tcf_demo}/src/demo.c:32

# 32:16 (the call of scale, stepped over), 32:13 (sum +=), 31:25 (i++), 31:19 (i < n).
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
expect i == 1
# From the condition back into the body: the second iteration.
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
expect i == 1
expect sum == 1
# Over the second call of scale (1 * 1 * 3 + 1 = 4): sum = 5 at i++.
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
step over 0
wait stopped 0 reason step
expect sum == 5
